1. Built with minimal JavaScript
This slider leans heavily on CSS to hide/ reveal slides,
making the implementation easy to understand. JavaScript
is necessary only to create functional next and previous
buttons. 

2. Use cases
I orginally built this slider to show off my resume online.
It could easily be modified to fit other common slider uses
such as testimonials, slideshows, products, or hero sections.

3. License 
This code is free to use by anyone without giving credit. There
is a hidden link in the html to my website (springcreekweb.design) 
that I kindly ask you to leave, but this is not required.

4. Setup 
To use the slider in your own website you simply need to copy the
code and extend it. These instructions assume you are using 
WordPress.org and have the ability to edit or extend your theme.
You will need a place to put custom JavaScript and CSS, this will
usually be within your theme/ child-theme. Simply copy the CSS and 
JS to the respective locations. The HTML can be added to either
a custom html block in the page editor, or to a custom page
template that you then asign to the slider page. 

5. Future/ Extending the Slider
The slider could be turned into a plugin without too much work,
and I may take the time to do this in the future. If this is 
something you'd be interested in, let me know!

